From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:30:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 619/619] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: give the USB11
 PHY the vendor squelch

Register dumps of the right USB-C port's PHY under the vendor kernel,
which enumerates a full-speed keyboard, and under mainline, where every
first control transfer fails with -EPROTO, differ in one control field:
the U2 squelch threshold, 8 against the driver's 2. Set 8 on the USB11
port only; the left port keeps the driver's value.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index a03c8a3f7..0f691f53b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -886,6 +886,12 @@ &usb11_tphy {
  * the controller is an A-device with VBUS present and starts its session.
  */
 &usb11_u2 {
+	/*
+	 * The vendor kernel leaves this receiver's squelch threshold at its
+	 * hardware default, 8. With the driver's 2, every control transfer to
+	 * a full-speed keyboard failed (station boot 28a5901c).
+	 */
+	mediatek,rx-sqth = <8>;
 	mediatek,force-b-session-valid;
 	status = "okay";
 };
